the target language is: prolog.

% =============================================================================
% A miniature DESIGN GRAMMAR: the front panel of a step sequencer.
%
% The knowledge base states what any playable step sequencer needs — a
% transport, a rhythm grid, a sound shaper — and the scenario lays out one
% concrete design, "my groovebox". Run query `design`, then right-click the
% answer and choose "Bento Box…": the explanation renders as the instrument
% itself — the outer box is the sequencer, the compartments are its panels,
% and the leaves are the knobs, buttons, pads and faders.
%
% Experiment: delete a control from the scenario (the design breaks — dark
% space where the panel was), move a knob to another panel, or add a rule for
% a panel of your own invention.
% =============================================================================

the templates are:
    *a device* is a playable step sequencer,
    *a device* has a working transport,
    *a device* has a rhythm grid,
    *a device* has a sound shaper,
    *a panel* is a panel of *a device*,
    *a control* is a button on *a panel*,
    *a control* is a knob on *a panel*,
    *a control* is a pad on *a panel*,
    *a control* is a slider on *a panel*.

the knowledge base sequencer includes:

a device is a playable step sequencer
    if the device has a working transport
    and the device has a rhythm grid
    and the device has a sound shaper.

% To start, stop and set the pace: a button and a tempo knob together on one panel.
a device has a working transport
    if a panel is a panel of the device
    and a control is a button on the panel
    and an other control is a knob on the panel.

% To write the rhythm: a row of pads on one panel.
a device has a rhythm grid
    if a panel is a panel of the device
    and pad one is a pad on the panel
    and pad two is a pad on the panel
    and pad three is a pad on the panel
    and pad four is a pad on the panel.

% To shape the sound: a fader for loudness and a knob for tone, side by side.
a device has a sound shaper
    if a panel is a panel of the device
    and a control is a slider on the panel
    and an other control is a knob on the panel.

scenario groovebox is:
    transport strip is a panel of my groovebox.
    step grid is a panel of my groovebox.
    mixer strip is a panel of my groovebox.

    run button is a button on transport strip.
    tempo dial is a knob on transport strip.

    pad one is a pad on step grid.
    pad two is a pad on step grid.
    pad three is a pad on step grid.
    pad four is a pad on step grid.

    volume fader is a slider on mixer strip.
    filter knob is a knob on mixer strip.

    design expects answers ["my groovebox is a playable step sequencer"].

query design is:
    which device is a playable step sequencer.
